## Recovered local application

- Requires Node.js 22 or newer. Run `npm ci` to install the locked dependencies for PDF generation and deployment. The local server itself uses Node built-ins; PDF creation uses pdf-lib and fontkit, bundled locally with esbuild.
- Run `npm start` from this repository, then open http://127.0.0.1:8787. Use `PORT=8788 npm start` if the default port is occupied.
- Run `npm test` for inventory/API tests and `npm run check` for JavaScript syntax checks.
- The [HTML interface](./html/index.html) lists all 210 drawers with separate number/position columns and editable title, description, tags and remark. Search covers those fields, drawer numbers and positions. Selecting a row or focusing a field displays the source photo on the right; drawer numbers are not buttons.
- Search also accepts a complete numeric range such as `90-96`, showing drawers **090 through 096 inclusive**. Leading zeros and spaces around the hyphen are accepted (`090 - 096`). Equal endpoints select one drawer; reversed ranges show no results. Other queries retain the existing case-insensitive, all-words text search. Select visible drawers can select the filtered range for PDF export; existing hidden selections are retained and counted.
- Editing and saving start locked, locally and on Cloudflare. Click **Enable editing** and enter the case-sensitive PIN `A1B2` once. Unlocking is remembered in browser `sessionStorage` for that tab session, including page refreshes and Reload; a fresh session starts locked again. Without the PIN, fields are read-only, Save now is disabled and no autosave is scheduled. Search, selection, photos, JSON export and PDF labels still work while locked.
- This PIN is deliberately visible in [app.js](./html/app.js): it prevents accidental edits, not unauthorized API access. It does not replace Cloudflare Access and cannot unlock a genuinely read-only backend. If browser session storage is unavailable, the interface reports the problem and keeps editing locked.
- PIN guard browser checks use a disposable inventory copy: cancelled/wrong PINs keep fields and saving locked; the correct PIN enables both five-second autosave and Save now, preserving exact whitespace. Page refresh and Reload keep the session unlocked. Read-only backend responses and unavailable session storage remain locked with explicit messages; search, selection and export remain available.
- Photos are visually transcribed from the supplied images, not sent to an external OCR service. Full-resolution originals remain in [photos](./photos); optimized display copies are in [html/images](./html/images). JSON `photo` paths are relative to the HTML directory. `sourceLabel` retains the initial reading and is not changed when editing inventory fields.
- Edits save after five seconds without typing in the same drawer. Editing another drawer does not postpone an earlier drawer's save. Save now bypasses the delay. Spaces and newlines are stored exactly; tags are comma-separated and spaces in each tag are preserved.
- The server writes [drawers.json](./drawers.json) atomically. Only the four editable fields can change. Concurrent changes to the same field are rejected with an explicit conflict, not silently overwritten. Edits remain in the browser on failure; use Save now to retry network failures. On a conflict, export your draft, reload, and reconcile the changed fields.
- Export JSON downloads the current inventory including unsaved edits. Reload asks before discarding drafts. Leaving the page with unsaved edits triggers the browser's warning; drafts are not automatically recovered after closing the browser.
- Stop the server before externally replacing or regenerating the JSON. Multiple browser tabs are supported through field-level conflict checks, but independent processes directly writing the file do not share the server's write queue.
- The server binds only to 127.0.0.1 and rejects foreign hosts/origins. It is not a public production backend.
- Multipage label PDF downloads are available; print them at Actual size (100%), not Fit to page.

## Compact list, selection and label draft

- Rows are 30 px high when all fields fit on one line. Every editable field wraps and automatically expands the row and its cells to fit its content, including after editing, filtering or changing the table width. Whitespace-preserving autosave is unchanged.
- Checkboxes toggle individual drawers. Clicking a number or position selects just that drawer; Ctrl/Cmd-click toggles it, Shift-click selects a range, and Ctrl/Cmd+Shift adds a range. Shift ranges contain only the current search results. Keyboard Space toggles a focused row; Enter selects it. Focusing or editing a text field previews its photo without changing the checkbox selection.
- The header checkbox selects/deselects visible results; hidden selections remain selected and are counted explicitly. Clear selection clears all checked drawers.
- **Download labels.pdf** creates one PDF page per selected drawer in inventory order, including selections hidden by filtering. It snapshots current values, including unsaved edits, without saving inventory or requiring the editing PIN. Every download requests the filename `labels.pdf`; the browser decides whether to replace an existing file or add a suffix.
- Labels are exactly **50 mm wide x 30 mm high**, with a white background and **1.5 mm inset print area**. The approved layout has a **46 x 9 mm** title box at (2, 2), centred bold title lines at y=6/10, uppercase description lines at (2, 16/19), a bold drawer number at (2, 28), and right-aligned position at (48, 27). Coordinates are millimetres measured from the top-left. Title wraps to 18 characters per line and description to 27, both limited to two lines with `...` for overflow. Tags and remarks are not printed; stored drawer text is untouched.
- All PDF text uses embedded **Noto Sans Mono Regular/Bold** (original font sizes retained), supplied locally under the SIL Open Font License in [html/fonts/LICENSE](./html/fonts/LICENSE). No external font service or PDF service is used. Missing fonts, download failures and unsupported characters produce an explicit error instead of a broken download.
- [html/label.js](./html/label.js) shares wrapping and content validation between editable SVG generation and the PDF renderer in [html/label-pdf.js](./html/label-pdf.js). `npm run build:labels` builds the ignored browser bundle; start, tests and Cloudflare build/deploy commands build it automatically.
- PDF validation: all 44 automated tests pass, including exact page dimensions, embedded fonts, wrapping/truncation, invalid records, unsupported glyphs, font-fetch errors and static asset serving. Browser checks cover PIN-locked export, hidden selections, draft export, repeat downloads, single-page output, empty selection and font-error retry. A three-page generated PDF was rendered and checked against the approved layout; all 210 current records also exported successfully.
- [label-template.svg](./label-template.svg) is the initial drawer-101 example to adapt in Vectorcraft and return as the next template.
- Validation: 21 automated tests pass. Browser checks measured exactly 30 px for a single-line row (including at device pixel ratio 1.5), verified all cells expand/shrink together on editing and width changes, exercised checkbox/Shift/Ctrl/keyboard selection, and confirmed one valid 50 x 30 mm SVG download with rendered text inside the 1.5 mm margins. Tests used a disposable inventory copy; original drawer data is unchanged.

